{"repositoryId":999848448,"availability":"available","full":"vexlin/ditherto","name":"ditherto","description":"Less colors, more vibes.  Pixelate your life by dithering your images to a fixed color palette.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":2,"forks":0,"created":"2025-06-10T22:12:01Z","updated":"2026-10-15T22:29:27Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://vexlin.github.io/ditherto/","topics":[],"demo":"https://vexlin.github.io/ditherto/playground.html","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:51:56.988Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T15:51:56.988Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T15:51:56.988Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T15:51:56.988Z","stars":2,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Dither images into a fixed palette, with optional resizing and tone adjustments. A TypeScript library for browsers, workers and Node, with a small PNG CLI and interactive examples.","Nine core algorithms: Atkinson, Floyd–Steinberg, Sierra Lite, Stucki, Bayer ordered dithering, Knoll, Halftone, Riemersma, and Nearest color. Two additional blue-noise variants are available through the optional ditherto/blue-noise entry. Bring your own palette or use black/white, monochrome red/green/blue/yellow, Game Boy, CGA, RGB, or 16-level grayscale.","Homepage · Image playground · Algorithm gallery · Why render live? · CLI guide · API"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vexlin/ditherto/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"80ae91271f9bb733695748dcf0cbda9392774ba34ea537b87c0c25d22b7e76ac","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T15:51:57.161Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T15:51:57.161Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Dither images into a fixed palette, with optional resizing and tone adjustments. A TypeScript library for browsers, workers and Node, with a small PNG CLI and interactive examples.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/vexlin/ditherto/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requ